WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.850
After a critically acclaimed and wildly successful
origin story, Wonder Woman is heading to 1984,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.100
and when she gets there, she'll find a new
foe lying in wait.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.660
Wonder Woman director Patty Jenkins has shared
the first official image of actress Kristen

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.520
Wiig in character on the set of Wonder Woman
1984, portraying the character Barbara Ann

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.880
Minerva, aka the villainous Cheetah.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.740
While it appears to be a look at Minerva in
her normal "80s lady" form, it's still cool

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.280
to see the character come to life, for the
first time ever in a live action film.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.120
Even if it DOES just look like a postcard
from a natural history museum, with Wiig standing

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.350
in a dark room, surrounded by exhibits.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.450
Dabbling in big-screen supervillainy is a
new career move for Wiig, who made a name

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.629
for herself in comedy with Saturday Night
Live and her Golden Globe-nominated turn in

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:45.129
Bridesmaids.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:50.640
She starred in the reboot of the Ghostbusters
franchise in 2016, but this is her first big

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.639
foray into the superhero genre.

00:00:52.639 --> 00:00:57.120
Cheetah's cinematic backstory is still unclear,
and in the comics, it varies quite a bit.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.579
In her first incarnation as Barbara Ann Minerva,
she's an ambitious archaeologist from a wealthy

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:03.870
family with a flexible moral compass.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:08.570
She gains supernatural powers while seeking
immortality from an ancient god of plants,

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:12.580
or by cutting herself on an ancient dagger,
or she's cursed, depending on which series

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.360
you read.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.020
In all of her incarnations, the transformation
leaves her in a tortured existence somewhere

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.080
between human and feline, her natural ambitions
supercharged by her immense new strength.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:27.400
Between this inspired casting and the expected,
but still unexplained return of Steve Trevor,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:31.860
Wonder Woman 1984 is shaping up to be among
the most interesting movies coming out of

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.300
Warner Bros. and DC in the near-future.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.960
Jenkins confirmed on Twitter earlier this
month that, despite sacrificing himself for

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.490
the safety of the entire world, Chris Pine's
Trevor will be in the Wonder Woman sequel.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.590
"Welcome to WONDER WOMAN 1984, Steve Trevor!"
Jenkins tweeted, along with a photo of Pine

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:53.420
looking totally '80s in era-appropriate clothes,
including what appears to be a Members Only

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:53.920
jacket.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.670
You'll remember that Trevor appeared to have
died at the end of the first Wonder Woman

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:02.190
flick, which was set in 1917 during World
War I, but it looks like he somehow went on

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.060
to live for another 67 years, and didn't age
a single day.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.080
Is this "Steve Trevor" a relative of the original
Steve Trevor?

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.920
Is there some sort of time travel in play?

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.600
Is a he just a stylish hallucination?

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.260
We'll have to wait and find out.

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:19.620
As a bonus treat, Wonder Woman herself, actress
Gal Gadot, also took to Twitter recently to

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.090
share a photo from the sequel.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:26.010
In it, Diana is seen staring at a wall of
screens, most of which display period-appropriate

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:31.100
shapes, colors, and stock images, but one
shows actor Larry Hagman as J.R. Ewing on

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.600
the 1980s primetime soap opera Dallas.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.890
From the original film's performance, we already
know the team behind this can make an excellent

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:38.640
superhero flick.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.940
Wonder Woman broke a ton of records in the
summer of 2017, becoming the highest-grossing

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:48.080
DC Extended Universe film ever at the domestic
box office, the most commercially successful

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.460
superhero origin story movie in history, and
the top-earning live-action film directed

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.440
by a woman.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:59.930
In total, the flick took home $821 million
worldwide and sits certified fresh with a

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.690
92 percent critical score and an 88 percent
audience rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:08.970
Speaking with Entertainment Tonight, Jenkins
promised that the sequel will be a completely

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.280
fresh experience compared to its predecessor.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.050
"It's not [Wonder Woman 2] to us.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.660
It's an entirely new adventure."

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.560
Wonder Woman 1984 will be out in theaters
on November 1, 2019.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.660
Thanks for watching!

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.840
